xtbox = page.get_by_role(\"textbox\", name=\"Name *\")\n    await name_textbox.fill(\"Test User\")\n    \n    # Fill the email field (assuming it has role 'textbox' and name 'Email *')\n    email_textbox = page.get_by_role(\"textbox\", name=\"Email *\")\n    await email_textbox.fill(\"test@example.com\")\n    \n    # Fill the website field if present (optional)\n    website_textbox = page.get_by_role(\"textbox\", name=\"Website\")\n    if await website_textbox.count() > 0:\n        await website_textbox.fill(\"\")\n    \n    # Check the 'Save my details' checkbox if present (assuming role 'checkbox' and name matching)\n    save_checkbox = page.get_by_role(\"checkbox\", name=\"Save my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment.\")\n    if await save_checkbox.count() > 0:\n        await save_checkbox.check()\n    \n    # Click the submit button (assuming role 'button' and name 'Post Comment')\n    submit_button = page.get_by_role(\"button\", name=\"Post Comment\")\n    await submit_button.click()\n    \n    # Wait for the submission to process\n    await page.wait_for_timeout(2000)\n    \n    # Return a success message\n    return \"Comment submitted successfully.\"\n</code>\n\n<result>\n'Comment submitted successfully.'\n</result>\n\n---\n\n<reasoning>\nI am currently on the 'Comment Submission Failure' page, as indicated by the accessibility tree showing a document with that title and a '\u00ab Back' link. My previous actions attempted to submit a comment on the target post, but it resulted in a submission failure. The task is to go to the post 'Settle Down, Nerds. AI Is A Normal Technology' and leave a comment saying 'Appreciate the detailed explanation.' Since the comment submission failed, I need to return to the post page to retry. The accessibility tree shows a link '\u00ab Back' with URL 'javascript:...'. Clicking this link should navigate back to the previous page, which is likely the post page. After returning, I can resubmit the co